started node adopts the snapshot's configuration whenever the newest configuration entry lies inside the skipped committed prefix (api.go 611-613 with 723-755, snapshot path api.go 645-689), and appendConfigurationEntry then computes the next configuration from that stale r.configurations.latest (raft.g\nanswers: {\"9c549c026d7341f2b1e328826eac6dc3-gap-0\": {\"explanation\": \"Yes for both parts, subject to the retained receipt for this probe: the stale configuration is adopted when the snapshot predates the committed configuration entry, and it does justify a different decision - a configuration change based on the stale membership drops voter C for the whole cluster (observed change_err=nil, both nodes ending\n{\n \"current\": {\n  \"phase\": \"executed\",\n  \"operation_id\": \"d2cb2558b564427ba5f166e377991a07\",\n  \"action\": \"update\",\n  \"no_change\": false,\n  \"references\": {\n   \"@restart_config\": \"9c549c026d7341f2b1e328826eac6dc3-question-0\"\n  },\n  \"experiment_id\": \"d2cb2558b564427ba5f166e377991a07-experiment\"\n },\n \"investigations\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"9c549c026d7341f2b1e328826eac6dc3-question-0\",\n   \"version\": 1,\n   \"question\": \"Does a node restarted with RestoreCommittedLogs=true, whose newest configuration entry is inside the persisted commit index and has no covering snapshot, still know that configuration after NewRaft returns?\",\n   \"hypothesis\": \"No. restoreFromCommittedLogs sets lastApplied to the persisted commit index, so the configuration scan starts after the committed prefix and never calls processConfigurationLogEntry for the configuration entry that only exists in the log. r.configurations.latest stays empty (or stays at the snapshot configuration), so the node loses its own membership context, cannot start elections, and skips the membership checks when granting votes.\",\n   \"discriminator\": \"Restart the same durable state twice: with RestoreCommittedLogs=true and with RestoreCommittedLogs=false. Predict servers_after=0 and no re-election with the feature on, versus servers_after=1 and a successful re-election with it off. A third run takes a snapshot before restart to show that a snapshot-carried configuration masks the loss (servers_after=1), separating the scanning bound from gener\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
