{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['sources'] += [\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"heartbeat_timeout_election\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":214,\\\"end_line\\\":251,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n]\nd['experiment']={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"9c549c026d7341f2b1e328826eac6dc3-question-0\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_quorum_restart_test.go\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"newraft_scan\\\",\\\"restore_committed\\\",\\\"follower_abort\\\",\\\"heartbeat_timeout_election\\\",\\\"cfg_doc\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Three-voter in-memory cluster {A,B,C} bootstrapped on A, all three running and converged on the configuration, ten commands committed, no snapshot ever taken (SnapshotThreshold huge, SnapshotInterval 10m). All three voters are then shut down and restarted at once on their own durable stores with fresh transports: case restore_on with RestoreCommittedLogs=true, control restore_off with it false. Observations: each node's configuration size (GetConfiguration), the number of nodes still holding the full configuration, and whether any leader is elected within a six-second opportunity (configured election/heartbeat timeouts are 50ms, so dozens of election windows).\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"Every voter shares the same durable history because A bootstrapped and replicated it; all three stores report a persisted commit index at or above the configuration entry index before the restart (observed: [11 11 9] against the configuration entry at index 1).\\\",\\\"No node snapshots before the restart, which is ordinary operation below SnapshotThreshold (8192 by default; the captured default SnapshotInterval is 120s).\\\",\\\"Simultaneous restart of all voters is a legal operator action, not a fault injection: every node is stopped gracefully and started with its documented configuration.\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"No partitions, no disk faults, no message loss; the only varying factor is RestoreCommittedLogs.\\\",\\\"The election fan-out itself is not traced beyond the observable absence of a leader and the logged 'no known peers, aborting election' path that source-reading identifies.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"protocol_version\\\":3,\\\"peers\\\":3,\\\"heartbeat_timeout_ms\\\":50,\\\"election_timeout_ms\\\":50,\\\"trailing_logs\\\":10,\\\"opportunity_seconds\\\":6}},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"Real bootstrap of all three voters on A's stores, real replication to B and C, real election, real applies, graceful shutdown of all three, then restart of all three on the same InmemCommitTrackingStore/InmemStore/InmemSnapshotStore instances with fresh in-memory transports. Nothing is fabricated: configuration, log and commit index all come from those operations; the control case repeats the identical procedure with RestoreCommittedLogs=false.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_all_on\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"pre_restart_restore_on\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_on\\\"}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_all_off\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"pre_restart_restore_off\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_off\\\"}]}\n ],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"post_restart_restore_on\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_all_on\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"nodes_with_full_config\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":3},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"After a simultaneous restart with RestoreCommittedLogs enabled, all three voters must still know the configuration whose entry is present in their own committed logs.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"post_restart_restore_off\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_all_off\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"nodes_with_full_config\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":3},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: the same simultaneous restart without RestoreCommittedLogs keeps all three voters configured, isolating the committed-prefix replay as the cause.\\\"}\n ]\n}\ni=d['interpretations'][0]\ni['conclusion']='violated'\ni['defect_claim']='asserted'\ni['executions']={'430d7ba602ed4666bdfe63a96c71e2fc':[1],'d2d1cb0951b74a2984ec525710e4c740':[1,3],'edfd3c204c654542a8bdb4263f290d4d':[1]}\ni['joint_history']=\\\"All receipts belong to this one question and to harnesses executed from the same snapshot. Receipt 430d7ba6 is the first restart probe (empty configuration, no snapshot); d2d1cb09 is the two-voter probe built afterwards to test the stale-configuration variant; edfd3c20 is the isolated control requested by the previous interpretation's own limitation, running the same single-voter restart with RestoreCommittedLogs=false so the control verdict is scored on its own event name.\\\"\ni['rationale']=(\\\"Three independent receipts, all retained. (1) 430d7ba602ed4666bdfe63a96c71e2fc index 1: with RestoreCommittedLogs=true and no snapshot the restarting node returns with an empty configuration (servers_after=0 against servers_before=1), never campaigns again in a 3s opportunity, and logs 'no known peers, aborting election'; both the non-replay run (index 3) and the snapshot run (index 5) keep the configuration and re-elect. (2) d2d1cb0951b74a2984ec525710e4c740 index 1: with a snapshot carrying {A,B}@1 and a committed AddVoter C at index 8 with staged commit 11, the restarted node reports 2 servers while its continuously running peer reports 3 and its own log still holds the newest configuration entry; index 3: a later AddVoter E then returns no error and both nodes converge on 3 members without C (contains_c_final=false), i.e. a legitimately added voter is silently removed from the cluster by a change computed from the stale base. (3) edfd3c204c654542a8bdb4263f290d4d index 1: the isolated control with RestoreCommittedLogs=false scores holds (servers_after=1 against the same bootstrapped voter), so the replayed committed prefix, not restart itself, is the cause. Source chain: restoreFromCommittedLogs raises lastApplied to the persisted commit index (api.go 723-755); the configuration scan then begins at max(lastSnapshot,lastApplied)+1 (api.go 611-613), so configuration entries inside the committed prefix are never fed to their only producer processConfigurationLogEntry (raft.go 1605-1623) unless a snapshot carries them (api.go 645-689). With Servers empty the follower refuses to campaign (raft.go 230-234 on every heartbeat timeout, raft.go 214-251) and both vote handlers skip their membership checks (raft.go 1663-1672, 1780-1784); with Servers stale, appendConfigurationEntry derives the next membership from that stale base (raft.go 1204-1241, configuration.go 224-302) once the admission gate sees latest==committed (raft.go 654-664).\\\")\ni['answers']={\\\"9c549c026d7341f2b1e328826eac6dc3-gap-0\\\":{\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Resolved by retained receipt d2d1cb0951b74a2984ec525710e4c740: the restarted node adopts the snapshot-carried configuration when the newest configuration entry lies inside the replayed committed prefix (comparison 0 violated, witness index 1: servers_after=2 while the peer reports 3 and the newest configuration entry index 8 is below the staged commit index 11), and that stale base changes a real decision (comparison 2 violated, witness index 3: AddVoter E returned no error and both nodes ended with 3 members and contains_c_final=false, so voter C was silently removed). The same receipt's control mode kept 3 members and ended with 4 including C (observed at parsed index 5; that comparison was scored unknown because both modes shared a result event name, which the dedicated control experiment has now replaced with a scored holds).\\\",\\\"resolved\\\":True}}\ni['counterevidence']=[\n \\\"The isolated control receipt edfd3c204c654542a8bdb4263f290d4d scores holds with the identical restart and no snapshot (servers_after=1), so the loss is caused by replaying the committed prefix, not by restart, snapshot absence, or the commit-tracking store.\\\",\n \\\"The snapshot run inside the first receipt (index 5) keeps the configuration, so the defect requires the newest configuration entry to be inside the skipped prefix; a snapshot taken after the change masks it.\\\",\n \\\"Voter C never runs in the two-voter probe, so nothing in the receipts shows C resisting or noticing its removal; the claim is about the configuration the running nodes decide with.\\\"]\ni['limitations']=[\n \\\"All executions are in-process in-memory clusters at protocol version 3 with 50ms heartbeat/election timeouts and a single committed configuration change; joint-consensus or multi-step changes are not exercised.\\\",\n \\\"The multi-node consequences that follow from an empty or stale Servers list (votes granted to servers the node cannot show it contains, cluster-wide unavailability after a simultaneous restart) are read from source here and are the subject of the cluster-restart experiment requested in this update.\\\",\n \\\"The finding is specific to RestoreCommittedLogs=true with a CommitTrackingLogStore; with the flag disabled the same durable state recovers normally.\\\"]\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\nEOF\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run; /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -5\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
